The server listens on `PORT` (default `3000`) and `HOST` (default `0.0.0.0`).
`LOG_LEVEL` accepts `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error`.

## Routes

| Method | Path | Response |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET/HEAD | `/` | Home page with the featured article |
| GET/HEAD | `/posts` | Complete archive |
| GET/HEAD | `/posts/:slug` | Article, or 404 |
| GET/HEAD | `/categories` | Category index |
| GET/HEAD | `/categories/:category` | Posts in a category, or 404 |
| GET/HEAD | `/tags/:tag` | Posts carrying a tag, or 404 |
| GET/HEAD | `/search?q=` | Search results |
| GET/HEAD | `/about` | About the publication |
| GET/HEAD | `/contact` | Contact details |
| GET/HEAD | `/feed.xml` | RSS 2.0 feed |
| GET/HEAD | `/api/health` | JSON health and content counts |
| GET/HEAD | `/api/posts` | JSON post summaries |
| GET/HEAD | `/api/posts/:slug` | JSON post, or 404 |
| GET/HEAD | `/assets/site.css` | Generated stylesheet |
| GET/HEAD | `/assets/favicon.svg` | Generated favicon |

Other methods on a known path return `405` with an `Allow` header. Unknown paths
return a real `404` page. `/blog`, `/blog/:slug`, `/post/:slug`, `/category/:slug`
and `/tag/:slug` permanently redirect to their canonical routes.

## Structure

```
src/
  app.ts            request pipeline: headers, redirects, dispatch, errors
  server.ts         executable entry point and graceful shutdown
  config.ts         site identity, contact address, PORT/HOST/LOG_LEVEL
  router/           route table and the framework-free router
  routes/           page and JSON controllers
  services/         content repository (search, taxonomy, related posts)
  content/          typed articles
  views/            HTML composition, RSS and the generated stylesheet
  middleware/       security headers, request logging, error handling
  lib/              escaping, response helpers, logging, slugs
test/
  router.test.ts    matching, canonical paths, method handling, conflicts
  routes.test.ts    every route, method, redirect, asset, API and error path
  links.test.ts     crawls every rendered page and fetches every internal link
  content.test.ts   sorting, search, taxonomy, related posts
```

## Editing

- Articles live in `src/content/posts.ts` and are typed. Use the block types in
  `src/domain/post.ts`; views escape every string.
- Site title, tagline and contact address live in `src/config.ts`. The generated
  contact address uses the reserved `.example` domain — replace it before you
  publish.
- The visual system comes from CSS custom properties in `src/views/styles.ts`.
  They were generated from the project's design tokens and are safe to edit.
- Adding a page means one view, one handler, one route registration and one
  route test. Adding a URL that is not registered is a 404 by design.

## Verification

`{{typecheckCommand}}` typechecks sources and tests. `{{testCommand}}` runs the
route suite against the real HTTP pipeline on an ephemeral port. `{{buildCommand}}`
emits `dist/`. Nothing is claimed as working that the tests do not exercise.
